// TEST: HMC Model Outside AD Subset (rejects)
// ERROR: BL5500
// ERROR-CONTAINS: if/else is not supported in differentiated code
import ppl as ppl
import ad as ad
// The plan's deliberate boundary probe: HMC coverage is bounded by the
// AD-able subset (src/Grad.fs:27-50) -- if/match in the MODEL is refused by
// grad itself, cleanly, when it differentiates the elaborator-emitted
// ad.grad(logpost) sites. ppl.logpdf/ppl.loglik model bodies stay inside
// the subset by construction; a hand-written branch does not. The refusal
// is BL5500 (grad elaboration), not BL5100: hmc's own guards pass -- the
// honest boundary is grad's. Note mh would accept this exact model (its
// sampler never differentiates), which is the documented mh/hmc split.
function lp(x: Float64) -> Float64 = if x > 0.0 then 0.0 - x else x
let c = ppl.hmc(lp, 0.0, 64, 0.5, 4, 7)
